Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,
I raise these question here, cause I think it might benefits others.
Regarding outliers, after using plotOutliers, I was wondering whether I should remove all red specimens/observations above the upper quartile, or only prominent outliers (how to decide?) or use something like this:
outliers = plotOutliers(A, groups = NULL)
iqr=1.5*IQR(outliers)
q1.iqr=quantile(outliers)[2]-iqr
q3.iqr=quantile(outliers)[4]+iqr
outliers.vec = as.vector(outliers[outliers>q3.iqr & outliers<q1.iqr])

in my case, using this code, I get no LM to be removed. Unlike the example in the guide, my red dots aren't separated as a distinct group, but run continuously as they were part of the data.
Is there any common practice/procedure/code to easily remove outliers LM?

Regarding switched LM, Is there any common practice/procedure/code to easily track and/or correct switched LM, or I have to go over each specimen/observation after using plotRefToTarget?

Many thanks,

Avi

