Does anyone know how to highlight the edges of a polygon (.ply) surface that opens in a rgl device while using geomorph? It is a very simple polygon which I wrote myself, but because of how it looks, it is hard to see shape changes: lighter lines (in the image, signed with red arrows) are the edges, but I would like to make them black.

I tried also editing the original ply file, but nothing happens. I can only add colors to the faces, but nothing happens to the edges. Is it even possible to do this? I am almost certain I did it accidentally a couple of days ago while playing with rgl.material arguments, but I did not record this, and as much as I try now, I get nothing.

